[h1]BBCode Preview[/h1]

Everything below renders live in the preview panel. Press [b]Ctrl+K V[/b]
([b]Cmd+K V[/b] on macOS) to open it beside the editor.

[h2]Text formatting[/h2]

[b]Bold[/b], [i]italic[/i], [u]underlined[/u] and [s]struck through[/s].
You can also write H[sub]2[/sub]O and x[sup]2[/sup].

[color=#e03131]Red[/color], [color=#2f9e44]green[/color] and
[bgcolor=yellow]highlighted[/bgcolor] text.

[size=150]Larger text[/size] and [size=85]smaller text[/size], plus
[font=Georgia]a different font[/font].

[h2]Quotes[/h2]

[quote="Alice" post=1234]
The best way to predict the future is to invent it.
[/quote]

[quote]
A quote without an attributed author.
[/quote]

[h2]Lists[/h2]

[list]
[*]Bulleted items need no closing tag
[*]The next item closes the previous one
[*]Nesting works too:
[list=a]
[*]Sub-item one
[*]Sub-item two
[/list]
[/list]

[list=1]
[*]First
[*]Second
[*]Third
[/list]

[h2]Code[/h2]

[code=js]
function greet(name) {
    return `Hello, ${name}!`;
}
[/code]

Inline code looks like [icode]npm install[/icode], and [noparse][b]this[/b][/noparse]
is shown verbatim.

[h2]Links and media[/h2]

A labelled link to [url=https://code.visualstudio.com]Visual Studio Code[/url],
a bare one: [url]https://github.com[/url], and an e-mail address:
[email]someone@example.com[/email].

[img width=320]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/microsoft/vscode/main/resources/linux/code.png[/img]

